=== 1. WHAT GOES WHERE - two tests, applied to every fact ===

TEST 1: "Would I be WRONG, or merely UNINFORMED, without this?"
  WRONG      -> stays inline in MEMORY.md. Prohibitions, scope, hard rules, credentials PATHS, IPs,
                the CIFS gotcha, "do not clean this up" warnings. Missing it causes DAMAGE.
  UNINFORMED -> phase file + a pointer row in MEMORY.md's PHASE INDEX. Missing it only means you
                have to go read something.

TEST 2: "Does this apply OUTSIDE the phase that produced it?"
  YES -> the DISTILLED PRINCIPLE goes in MEMORY.md (one or two lines), the 300-line narrative of how
         it was discovered goes in the phase file. Keep the rule, not the story.
         Examples: false greens; one instrument per question; reachable is not usable; probe the
         capability you are about to use, not a proxy; severity should match consequence.
  NO  -> phase file only.

MEMORY.md (static, project-wide reference):
- IPs, credential file PATHS (never the credentials themselves), commands, architecture
- Prohibitions and directives - anything whose absence causes damage
- Key decisions and WHY
- The PHASE INDEX (pointer table) - keep it current when a phase is added or closed
- Distilled cross-phase principles
- Update only if infrastructure/config/policy changed

phases/current_phase.md (session progress):
- ONE "▶️ RESUME HERE" block at the top: current phase, goal, state, next steps, blockers
- ONE current session handoff
- Include explanations if YOU need them to understand later

phases/phaseX_*.md (the working record - where the volume belongs):
- Drills, predictions and their scoring, raw evidence, per-session narrative, ledgers


=== 2. DEMOTION (the step that was missing) ===

Do this whenever EITHER is true: a phase closes, or the size report in step 0 makes you wince.

  a. Pick the largest block in MEMORY.md's CURRENT STATE belonging to a CLOSED or dormant phase.
  b. Confirm the phase file already covers it:  rg '<a distinctive phrase>' phases/phaseX_*.md
     If it does NOT, COPY the content there FIRST and verify it landed before deleting anything.
  c. Replace the block in MEMORY.md with a PHASE INDEX row (see format below).
  d. VERIFY, from the shell, not from a read-back (this repo is on CIFS - see MEMORY.md gotcha):
       wc -l MEMORY.md
       git diff MEMORY.md | rg '^-' | rg -v '^---'     # read EVERY removed line
     Every deleted line must be one you meant to delete AND must now exist in the phase file.
  e. COMMIT before demoting the next block, so any loss is one `git show` away.

🚨 Silent loss of a hard-won finding is the worst failure mode this project has. One block at a
time, verified, committed between steps. Never batch demotions.

Also demote from current_phase.md: when a new session starts, the PREVIOUS session handoff is
appended to its phase file and removed from current_phase.md. It holds ONE handoff.


